  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "Triangle \\(ABC\\) has a right angle at \\(B.\\) Point \\(D\\) is the foot of the altitude from \\(B,\\) \\(AD = 3,\\) and \\(DC = 4.\\) What is the area of \\(\\triangle ABC?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(4\\sqrt{3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(7\\sqrt{3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(21\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(14\\sqrt{3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(42\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2009-p10.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For the altitude from the right angle to the hypotenuse, \\[BD^2 = AD \\cdot DC = 3 \\cdot 4 = 12,\\] so \\(BD = 2\\sqrt{3}.\\)\n\nThe hypotenuse is \\(AC = 3 + 4 = 7,\\) so the area is \\[\\dfrac12 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 2\\sqrt3 = 7\\sqrt3.\\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "The altitude to the hypotenuse satisfies \\(BD^2 = AD \\cdot DC\\)",
        "The hypotenuse is \\(AC = AD + DC = 7\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
